{{/*
  404.html.tmpl — dist/404.html.

  Built by renderNotFound (build.go), NOT by the pages loop in Run: it must
  never contribute a Path to the sitemap. Dot is a notFoundPage, which embeds
  page directly (no wrapper type beyond that) — same pattern as
  about.html.tmpl and legal.html.tmpl, plus its own NoIndex field that always
  overrides page's site-derived one to true (see notFoundPage's doc comment
  in build.go).

  Content is a short signpost, not an essay: the site's editorial voice,
  pointing back at the two places a lost visitor actually wants — the
  portfolio and a way to get in touch.
*/}}
{{define "404"}}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{{template "head" .}}
</head>
<body>
{{template "header" .}}
<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">404</span>
      <h1>This page has left the cellar.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The page you're looking for isn't here &mdash; it may have moved, or the address
        wasn't quite right. From here, the full portfolio is the surest way onward, and the team is
        always glad to help you find what you're after.</p>
      <p class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/portfolio/">Browse the Portfolio</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact/">Contact Us</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
{{template "footer" .}}
</body>
</html>
{{end}}
